{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Phase 4 (understandingloop.md): the epistemic work queue, derived from claim state - no LLM, no randomness. Domains are read as the facet+overlay union (one-memory-cycle), so curation surfaces the moment it happens. stale (3): source hash drifted, unacknowledged - the one kind the executive may act on (decay). review (2): confidence at the low floor or drift acknowledged - surfaced for humans. plan (accepted/in-progress at 4/3, proposed at 1): active INTENT from kb.plan, lifecycle in tags (done/abandoned/completed surface as nothing) - surfaced, never auto-executed. SUB-ITEMS: a kb.plan entry that is a PARENT (another entry points at it via `parent`) is suppressed as a container - its children are the unit of work and surface instead; it re-surfaces only if childless, and reports done via step_item's rollup once all children are done. unpromoted (1): subject-bearing brain claims NOT yet stamped promoted. Returns {items (top 20), stale, review, unpromoted, plan, total}. Read-only.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;\nuse flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;","params":[],"returntype":"JSONObject","type":"rust"},"id":"ixhqrg1a0068b1a0cx1","readers":[],"time":1792758402557,"username":"system","writers":[]}